  "question": {
    "text": "Choose the correct nuclear process from the below options\n[p: proton, n : neutron, $\\mathrm{e}^{-}$: electron, $\\mathrm{e}^{+}$: positron, $v:$ neutrino, $\\bar{v}$ : antineutrino]",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "SVWlK",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{n} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{p}+\\mathrm{e}^{+}+\\bar{v}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SKVmd",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{n} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{p}+\\mathrm{e}^{+}+\\boldsymbol{v}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "R8Uj4",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{n} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{p}+\\mathrm{e}^{-}+\\boldsymbol{v}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "nVCiW",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{n} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{p}+\\mathrm{e}^{-}+\\bar{v}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For all nuclear processes, charge must be conserved. Also, when a release of an electron ( $e^{-}$) is always accompanied by a release of an antineutrino ( $\\bar{v}$ )\n\nHence, $n \\rightarrow p+\\mathrm{e}^{-}+\\overline{\\mathrm{v}}$ is the correct answer.",
    "image": null
  },
